  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-04-09T19:31:17.823Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The new update changed a lot of mechanics related to jumping. While the inability to glide in certain Udon worlds isn't too big of a deal (gliding was kind of glitchy anyways), one change that's been extremely frustrating is that jump buffering has been patched out of the game.\nIn versions of VRChat before the big update, the user could press the jump button while descending from a jump, and they would automatically jump again once they hit the ground. This made traveling long distances and little bits of parkour a little easier and more pleasing. Now, however, pressing the jump button when descending from a jump does nothing, which makes jumping around a good bit more difficult and less satisfying. Could we get jump buffering back please?",
